---
// The cookie pop-up: Reject all and Accept, equally prominent. Hidden in the
// markup and shown by script only when no choice is stored, so it never
// shifts the page. Fixed to the foot of the window, clear of the result.
---

<div class="cookie-banner" data-cookie-banner role="region" aria-label="Cookies" hidden>
	<p>We would like to use Google Analytics cookies to count visits. Nothing you type into a calculator is ever sent, whichever you choose. <a href="/privacy/#cookies">More about cookies</a></p>
	<div class="cookie-actions">
		<button type="button" data-cookie-reject>Reject all</button>
		<button type="button" data-cookie-accept>Accept</button>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.cookie-banner {
		position: fixed;
		left: 0;
		right: 0;
		bottom: 0;
		z-index: 20;
		background: var(--page);
		border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
		padding: 0.9rem var(--gutter);
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
	}
	.cookie-banner[hidden] { display: none; }
	.cookie-banner p { margin: 0; max-width: 46rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
	.cookie-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; }
	.cookie-actions button { min-width: 7.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
	@media print { .cookie-banner { display: none !important; } }
</style>
